  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) Assessed Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Department of Health and Aged Care&apos;s assessed contribution (membership fees) to the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) allows Australia to actively participate in the IARC through its Governing Council. The IARC Governing Council sets the international agenda for cancer prevention and control including setting priorities through IARC&#x2019;s program of permanent activities. On 28 April 2020, the OECD&#x2019;s Development Assistance Committee Working Party on Development Finance Statistics (WP-STAT) members approved the proposal to add IARC to the list of ODA-eligible international organisations. 51% of the assessed contributions paid to the IARC are ODA-eligible.</narrative>
  </description>
